{
  "assessment": "The task requires recursively cloning nested objects and arrays so that every level is independent of the original. The diff replaces the file with a shallow-copy implementation: `Array.map(v => v)` creates a new array but keeps references to its elements, and `{ ...value }` spreads an object while copying property values by reference. It handles primitives correctly, stops at the first nesting level, and fails to recurse into nested structures.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "clone.a[0].b becomes 99; original is mutated because arrays/objects are shared references",
      "at": "solution.ts:3-4 (array branch) and solution.ts:5-6 (object branch)",
      "call": "node -e \"import {deepClone} from './solution'; const orig = {a: [{b: 2}]}; const clone = deepClone(orig); clone.a[0].b = 99; console.log(orig.a[0].b === 1 ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL');\"",
      "defect": "Shallow copy instead of recursive deep copy",
      "expected": "original remains unchanged (prints PASS)"
    }
  ]
}
